# Volkswagen Polo Mk6 (Typ AW) five-door hatchback, 2018-2024.
#
# The AW Polo: a wider, lower body than the Mk5, with a sharper shoulder line,
# a horizontal grille and swept headlamps. The pre-facelift 2018 car is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volkswagen_Polo_Mk6
#
# Dimensions 4.053 x 1.751 x 1.446 m, wheelbase 2.548 m.
#
# Shape reference: a true level side elevation of a 2019 SEL TSI, plus front
# and rear three-quarters and a detail. The 2019 SEL and the 2018 SE are two
# different red UK cars; the side is the 2019 SEL.
#
# Colours: grade (d), no UK brochure retrieved. White, Grey, Black and Blue are
# plain colour names. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total 30, provisional pending the
# central rebase.
#
# Speed 200 km/h. Comfort 80/450, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 80. Classes 1,2.
# Dates orders October 2017, deliveries January 2018, to October 2024; road
# tail staggered 2039-2042.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vw-polo-mk6.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vw-polo-mk6.dae. References: citycars/references/vw-polo-mk6/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the SEL side governed the body. The roof crown is flatter,
# the window corners more angular and the shoulder crease less pronounced than
# the photographs; door seams and wheel spokes are not represented. The nose,
# lamp inserts and lower valance are simplified. The facelift is not modelled.
# The spoiler passes Stage B in connectivity mode, attached to the hatch.


